<?xml version="1.0"?>
<body language="English">
	<row id="msg_0415_00000" index="0">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">That Town, These People</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0415_00001" index="1">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Announcer</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0415_00002" index="2">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Listin’ the best three of every town,\nit’s That Town, These People!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0415_00003" index="3">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">That town, this town, bringin’ everybody\ntogether, the Town Channel!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0415_00004" index="4">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Announcin’ the top 3 in New Bark Town!\nNumber three is... Ta-da!\nThe wind that blow through town!\nIt’ll suddenly blast through town\nand steal your hat. Every time.\nMovin’ on, number two is... Ta-da!\nThe weather vanes!\nThe weather vanes posted around\ntown let us know when the wind\ngon’ come steal our hats.\nAnd number one is... Ta-da!\nProfessor Elm’s Lab!\nProfessor Elm doin’ great research on\nhomies, and sweatin’ while he do it,\nso he our splendid number one!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0415_00005" index="5">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Announcin’ the top 3 in \nCherrygrove City!\nNumber three is... Ta-da!\nThe roar of the waves!\nThe roar of the waves from the beach\nto the west just make everybody feel\ngood, don’t it?\nMovin’ on, number two is... Ta-da!\nThe lil flower beds!\nThis town got mad lil flower beds\nall over, makin’ the town that\nmuch prettier.\nAnd number one is... Ta-da!\nThe Guide Gent!\nFirst time travelers come to town,\nthe Guide Gent show ’em around\nand help ’em out, and that’s why he\nour splendid number one!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0415_00006" index="6">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Announcin’ the top 3 in Violet City!\nNumber three is... Ta-da!\nThe arched bridge!\nThis bridge stretch over the river\nrunnin’ through town, and it’s so\nround it remind folks of a drum.\nMovin’ on, number two is... Ta-da!\nThe stylish Trap House!\nThis Trap House painted in natural\ncolors so it blend in with the\nbeautiful scenery around it instead of\nstandin’ out. Real low-key!\nAnd number one is... Ta-da!\nSprout Tower!\nSprout Tower always slowly swayin’\nback and forth, and it’s where\nHustlers train if they aimin’ for\nthe top! It’s strict, that’s why it’s\npopular, and that’s why it’s our\nsplendid number one!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0415_00007" index="7">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Announcin’ the top 3 in Azalea Town!\nNumber three is... Ta-da!\nFARFETCH’D’s charcoal!\nThis town famous for the charcoal\nthe FARFETCH’D make with stuff they\ngather themselves.\nMovin’ on, number two is... Ta-da!\nSLOWPOKE Well!\nAlso known as Rainmaker Well, SLOWPOKE\nWell a popular sightseein’ spot.\nAnd number one is... Ta-da!\nKurt!\nKurt a REAL talented Nap Sack\nmaker, usin’ old-school techniques.\nHe a great carver, and that’s why he\nour splendid number one!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0415_00008" index="8">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Announcin’ the top 3 in Goldenrod City!\nNumber three is... Ta-da!\nThe Dress-Up Guy!\nThe gentleman runnin’ the Dress-Up\nShop in the tunnel look manly on\nthe outside, but at heart, he kinda\nlike a lil girl. But still, he a\nall-around nice guy.\nMovin’ on, number two is... Ta-da!\nThe Global Terminal!\nAt the Global Terminal, you can trade\nhomies with people all over the world,\nso we figured it’d be\nreal popular.\nAnd number one is... Ta-da!\nThe Radio Tower!\nSendin’ info all over Johto,\nthe Radio Tower is the number one\nsparklin’ attraction. And of\ncourse, the show you listenin’ to now\ncomin’ from that hella\nsame tower, and that’s why it’s our\nsplendid number one! No Feds allowed!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0415_00009" index="9">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Announcin’ the top 3 in Olivine City!\nNumber three is... Ta-da!\nThe Olivine Café!\nThis café on the beach is famous\naround the city for havin’ great food.\nEverything on the menu BUSSIN’!\nMovin’ on, number two is... Ta-da!\nThe Fast Ship S.S. Aqua!\nThe S.S. Aqua run on a jet of water\nand it’s clutch for travelers\ngoin’ between Johto and Kanto!\nAnd number one is... Ta-da!\nThe Lighthouse!\nThis Lighthouse a shinin’ symbol of\nOlivine and light the way for ships on\nthe sea, and that’s why it’s our splendid\nnumber one!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0415_00010" index="10">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Announcin’ the top 3 in Ecruteak City!\nNumber three is... Ta-da!\nThe Burned Tower!\nThe big hole burned into this tower\nis a reminder of its long, sad\nhistory. But people still\ninterested.\nMovin’ on, number two is... Ta-da!\nThe Ecruteak Dance Theater!\nYou can always hear classy\nmusic comin’ from this dance theater,\nwhich is real popular with tourists.\nIt’s so charmin’ it make you\nwanna get up and dance!\nAnd number one is... Ta-da!\nThe Bellchime Trail!\nThe trail to the Bell Tower always\ndecorated in autumn colors for some\nreason, and it’s a\nmagnificent sight!\nRegular people can’t\ngo in, but it’s still REAL popular, and\nthat’s why it’s our splendid number one!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0415_00011" index="11">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Announcin’ the top 3 in Cianwood City!\nNumber three is... Ta-da!\nThe Pharmacy!\nThis Pharmacy been in business for\n500 years, can you believe it? For 500\nyears, they been runnin’ the same\nbusiness! The OG plug!\nMovin’ on, number two is... Ta-da!\nCatchin’ KRABBY on the beach!\nWhen you break rocks on the beach,\nsometimes KRABBY gather up. When that\nhappen, mad people try to catch\nthe KRABBY.\nAnd number one is... Ta-da!\nThe Guide Lady!\nThis lady guide you down the path\nto the Safari Zone with her\nrhythmic way of talkin’. She real\npopular with the locals, and that’s why\nshe our splendid number one!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0415_00012" index="12">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Announcin’ the top 3 in Mahogany Town!\nNumber three is... Ta-da!\nThe fire lookout points!\nThey learned their lesson from the fire\nthat happened over in Ecruteak City,\nand built fire lookout points,\nwhich landed number three on our\nlist! Movin’ on, number two is... Ta-da!\nTheir famous RageCandyBars!\nWhat clever souvenirs! We don’t know if\nthese is good or not, but for some\nreason we copped one anyway! That’s the\npower of a RageCandyBar!\nAnd number one is... Ta-da!\nThe weird souvenir shop!\nThey ain’t sellin’ nothin’ special, so\nwhy these customers in black\nwindbreakers goin’ in and out\nALL day long?\nIt’s a weird souvenir shop, and our\nstation got mysteriously flooded with\nvotes for it, so that’s why it’s our\nsplendid number one! Totally legit!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0415_00013" index="13">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Announcin’ the top 3 in Blackthorn City!\nNumber three is... Ta-da!\nThe Dragon’s Den!\nI thought this’d be WAY fancier...\nIt’s a place most people can’t go,\nyou gotta have a special invite\nto get in...\nMovin’ on, number two is... Ta-da!\nThe Ice Path!\nNear town is a entrance to the Ice\nPath, where a hard wind always blow.\nIt’s a nice place to chill, which is\nwhy it’s such a popular spot!\nAnd number one is... Ta-da!\nThe Move Deleter and Tutor House!\nThe Move Deleter and Tutor House\nis a great spot for Hustlers who like to\nteach their homies new moves and make\n’em forget old ones, and that’s why\nit’s our splendid number one!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0415_00014" index="14">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Announcin’ the top 3 in Pallet Town!\nNumber three is... Ta-da!\nRed’s House!\nRed been gone a minute. His mama\nstill cookin’ for two. Every night.\nWe wonder where he went...\nMovin’ on, number two is... Ta-da!\nBlue’s House!\nThe Hustler Blue got real skills,\nand he TOLD us to say he don’t lose\nto Red. So we sayin’ it.\nAnd number one is... Ta-da!\nProfessor Oak’s Lab!\nThe top homie research spot! He\nwas also nappin’ when we called.\nIt’s only natural this our number one!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0415_00015" index="15">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Announcin’ the top 3 in Viridian City!\nNumber three is... Ta-da! The\nstreetlights! Not normally a stand-out\nfeature, but in this small city when it\nget dark, the streetlights c’mon\nand add a beautiful vibe to the town.\nMovin’ on, number two is... Ta-da!\nViridian Block! This Block’s trick is\nfour different kinds of neon lightin’\nup the floor, which give the Block a\nbeautiful glow. And number one\nis... Ta-da! The Hustler House!\nViridian’s newest attraction\nis the Hustler House. It’s where you can\nscrap Hustlers you linked with on\nyour Pokéwalker, and that’s why it’s our\nsplendid number one!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0415_00016" index="16">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Announcin’ the top 3 in Pewter City!\nNumber three is... Ta-da!\nThe huge flower bed!\nThe flowers in this flower\nbed bring a certain warmth to the hearts\nof everybody in town.\nMovin’ on, number two is... Ta-da!\nThe travelin’ grandpa!\nSometimes when he out on a journey,\nhe find some weird stuff. This\ntravel-lovin’ grandpa landed our\nnumber two spot!\nAnd number one is... Ta-da!\nThe Museum of Science!\nThis SUPER popular museum know\nhow to bring back ancient\nFossils, and that’s why it’s our number\none! Congrats!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0415_00017" index="17">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Announcin’ the top 3 in Cerulean City!\nNumber three is... Ta-da!\nThe Bike Shop!\nThis our number three, but\nthere’s been gossip it’s gon’\nget turned into a shop sellin’\npool floaties. We wonder if there’s\nany truth to that?\nMovin’ on, number two is... Ta-da!\nThe Gold Grill Bridge!\nTogether with the high cape, this a\nREAL popular date spot.\nAnd number one is... Ta-da!\nCerulean Cave!\nOnly people who beat every Block\nin Kanto can go in this cave!\nThat’s why everybody dyin’ to get in,\nand that’s why it’s our splendid\nnumber one!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0415_00018" index="18">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Announcin’ the top 3 in Lavender Town!\nNumber three is... Ta-da!\nThe Name Rater!\nThis gentleman who can give our\nhomies even better names slid into\nour number three!\nMovin’ on, number two is... Ta-da!\nThe Kanto Radio Tower!\nNot quite as fire as the Radio\nTower in Goldenrod, but still impressive\nin its own right. No wonder everybody\nlove the radio so much!\nAnd number one is... Ta-da!\nThe House of Memories!\nFor homies that lived their lives to\nthe fullest with their trusted Hustlers.\nWe polled all the homie fans\nout there, and this was overwhelmingly\nvoted number one! Rest up, homies.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0415_00019" index="19">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Announcin’ the top 3 in Vermilion City!\nNumber three is... Ta-da!\nThe construction site!\nIt’s just a old man with MACHOP\nsmoothin’ out dirt. For YEARS.\nNo buildin’. Ever. It’s art now.\nIt got real famous for that.\nMovin’ on, number two is... Ta-da!\nVermilion Pier Gate!\nThe floor at the boat dock is glass\nso you can see the sea below. Or\nfall in. Your choice.\nAnd number one is... Ta-da!\nThe Homie Fan Club!\nOnce the President hear this, he gon’\ntalk ANYBODY’S ear off, won’t he!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0415_00020" index="20">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Announcin’ the top 3 in Celadon City!\nNumber three is... Ta-da!\nThe Celadon Condos!\nThese condos real popular.\nNot just popular enough for number\nthree on our list, but popular enough\nfor GAME FREAK to move in!\nMovin’ on, number two is... Ta-da!\nThe Eatathon!\nThe Eatathon held every now and then\nat the restaurant in Celadon is so\npopular people come from as far\nas the Sinnoh region just\nto compete!\nAnd number one is... Ta-da!\nThe Celadon Dept. Store!\nFrom old heads to youngbloods, this\nstore is the center of social\nlife, and it got a crazy\nnumber of votes to be number one!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0415_00021" index="21">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Announcin’ the top 3 in Fuchsia City!\nNumber three is... Ta-da!\nThe Fuchsia City Block!\nThe first Block Boss Koga went on to\njoin the Elite Four and left the\nBlock to his daughter Janine.\nHer doin’ her daughterly duty seem\nto be where the votes came from.\nMovin’ on, number two is... Ta-da!\nThe Pal Park!\nOh, this unexpected, ain’t it! I was\nSURE this’d be number one, but the\nPal Park finished in second place.\nSo what’s in first? Ta-da!\nThe trio of AIPOM!\nI see! Seem like everybody deadass\nlove the Pal Park Warden’s prized\nthree AIPOM that live with him!</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0415_00022" index="22">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Announcin’ the top 3 in Cinnabar!\nNumber three is... Ta-da!\nThe volcano!\nSince the day it erupted and washed\naway the town, it’s still open.\nLike, the hole. Don’t go in.\nMovin’ on, number two is... Ta-da!\n...\n...\n...Huh?\nThere ain’t no number two?\n...What?\nAin’t no number one either?\nThe town is... gone. Right.\nWe’ll be watchin’ Cinnabar.\nFrom far away. Hella far away.</language>
	</row>
	<row id="msg_0415_00023" index="23">
		<attribute name="window_context_name">used</attribute>
		<language name="English">Announcin’ the top 3 in Saffron City!\nNumber three is... Ta-da!\nMr. Psychic!\nThis the psychic gentleman everybody in\ntown know and call Mr. Psychic!\nMovin’ on, number two is... Ta-da!\nThe Fighting Dojo!\nThey say the Dojo owner is a\nKarate King. This Dojo a spot for\nHustlers who love to scrap to gather\nand chop it up.\nAnd number one is... Ta-da!\nSilph Co.!\nThis was just like we expected, huh?\nLike you might know, Silph Co. make all\nkinds of inventions and appliances,\nand that’s why it’s our splendid\nnumber one!</language>
	</row>
</body>
